## Respond (optional)

`/compathy-respond` keeps its companion files in `context/respond/`:

```
context/respond/
├── policy.md           human-owned; who, triggers, sources, links, never, tiers, limits
├── sources.md          human-owned; the registry of shareable documents
├── lessons.md          co-evolved; house answers, do-not-answer, clarify-first, phrasing, gaps
├── ledger.md           append-only; one entry per interaction (local, never shared)
├── handoff-<date>.md   written when a window stops
└── .respond-state.json window, last-seen, handled keys, counters
```

Frontmatter types: `respond-policy`, `respond-registry`, `respond-lessons`,
`respond-ledger`, `respond-handoff`. Flat YAML as everywhere else. The
stand-in reads the wiki; it never writes `wiki/` or `raw/`. Lint checks the
folder's structure when it exists (warnings only).
